# Production author allowlist (CONTEXT_BINDING_FAIL_CLOSED / PROD/TEST ENV
# SEPARATION, PR #19 closeout).
#
# The watcher in production reads this file via --author-allowlist (or its
# default location under the host's config dir) when --env=prod. When the
# file is MISSING, the CLI fails closed (exit code != 0 + stderr message).
#
# Fail-closed-by-default: this file ships with ONLY ``neokyhurtado-cmd``
# (David) as an allowed author. ``astra`` is intentionally NOT in the
# default prod allowlist because the production watcher must only accept
# directives from David; Astra's re-audits come through David in the
# governance process, not through the watcher's auto-execution path.
#
# To add an author, append a new ``- <login>`` line below. GitHub logins
# are case-insensitive in the match; list them in canonical lowercase.
allowlisted_authors:
  - neokyhurtado-cmd